course: dictionary
lesson: 8305
title: One word, many meanings: road
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can mean different things in different places. Road is a good example. Its main meaning is a wide hard path where cars, buses and bikes travel from one place to another, but it also appears in phrases. Look at the words around it to work out which meaning the writer means.
explain: «His shoulders humped, his eyes fixed on the straight grey road.» Here road means the actual path, because the Rat is walking along it and the clues are straight and grey. Now try: «We are going on a road trip.» Here road means a journey by car, not a path. Always ask what road is doing in the sentence.
explain: Some phrases use road in a special way. «On the road» means travelling. «Down the road» means near or later. «The road to success» means the way to reach success. Do not look for a hard path or a car in these phrases: the clues are in the whole phrase.
fact: A road is a wide hard path where cars, buses and bikes travel from one place to another.
fact: «Road» is part of many street names, such as «12 Mill Road».
fact: «On the road» means travelling.
fact: The road to something is the way to reach it, as in «the road to success».
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word the writer wants: read the words around it before you decide.
exercise: «A girl in Dublin always left in a rush and ran across the road to catch the bus.» In this sentence, what does road mean? | *A wide hard path where buses and cars travel | Travelling for fun | The way to reach a goal | A street name
exercise: Mia says, «We are on the road all summer.» What does on the road mean? | Asleep in the car | Standing still at the side of the path | *Travelling from place to place | Lost in the countryside
exercise: «Sam lives at 12 Mill Road.» What is road doing in this address? | *Part of a street name | A journey by car | Something that rusts | The way to reach success
test: «Salt from gritted winter roads makes iron rust faster, so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly.» In this sentence, what do roads mean? | *Wide hard paths where cars travel | The way to reach winter | Gritted pieces of bread | Long journeys by bike
test: Ella says, «The road to a good job is hard work.» What does road to mean here? | A street name in town | A wide hard path for cars | *The way to reach a good job | Travelling for work
exam: «His eyes fixed on the straight grey road» is from a book about two animals walking. Which meaning of road is used, and what clue shows it? | *A wide hard path, because the Rat is walking along it and it is straight and grey | A street name, because it is grey | The way to success, because the Rat wants to get home | A journey by car, because straight roads are for cars
